The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tb[NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN])
    return -EBUSY;
```
Reason:
This code immediately returns an `-EBUSY` error if the `NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN` attribute is present, without checking whether the size of the private helper data has actually changed. This results in updates with the same size being incorrectly rejected, leading to false positives.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
size = ntohl(nla_get_be32(tb[NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN]));
if (size != helper->data_len)
    return -EBUSY;
```
Reason:
These statements first retrieve the size of the private helper data from the attribute and then compare it to the existing size. The `-EBUSY` error is only returned if the sizes differ, allowing updates with the same size to proceed correctly, thus fixing the issue of false positives.

